# Exclusion patch notes, newest first (shown in the launcher's news panel).
# Format: "## Title | Date" starts an entry; "- " bullet; other lines are paragraphs; **bold** *italic* `code`.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.8 | 2026-11-03
A patch: no block-game pop-ups, slower rats, proper ladder climbing and a working head torch.
- **No more block-game pop-ups:** no skill, Exploring, discovery or achievement notices in the Zone, and no death compass.
- **Rad rats are slower:** sprint and you can outrun the swarm.
- **Ladders:** the gun is slung while you climb, two hands on the rungs.
- **Head torch:** wear it in the new LAMP slot, switch it with L / d-pad up.
- **Main menu music** is the Zone's quiet mood now.
- **Gun sounds:** no more empty sound for a gun without a sound class.
- Removed Herobrine.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.7 | 2026-11-03
A patch: solid foundations, a new ending place and a louder plant.
- **No more houses on stilts:** short gaps under buildings are filled with stone or concrete foundations.
- **The story ends at the Generators:** follow the Ferryman past the plant, over the river.
- **Emissions near the plant** hit earlier and harder at CNPP and the Generators.
- **The Generators' energy spheres hum** as you come near.
- Removed Herobrine.

## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.6 | 2026-11-03
Your Zone: the map is rebuilt from your own hand-made Zone, at S.T.A.L.K.E.R. Anomaly scale.
- **Every place:** from the Great Swamps and Cordon to Pripyat, CNPP and the Generators, with the STALKER names, joined by roads.
- **Life:** campfire camps, bandit posts, checkpoints, mutant lairs, squads on the roads and anomaly fields near the start.
- **Looting like the games:** wardrobes, fridges, lockers and desks to search, crates to smash, items on tables and shelves. No chests.
- **Animations:** weapon sway, sprint, aim, recoil, reloads, Misery-style eating and bandaging; stalkers at low ready and round campfires; mutant gaits.
- **Real scale** for every item, two-block beds, denser overgrowth.
- Removed Herobrine.

## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.5 | 2026-11-03
The Real Zone: the world from a satellite map, people to talk to, work to do and anomalies that kill.
- **The real layout:** the plant, the cooling pond, Pripyat, the Red Forest, the villages, rivers, lake and railway, with roads joining everything.
- **Talk, trade and work:** rumours, jobs from traders and camp leaders, lootable bodies and stashes, factions that remember.
- **Twenty anomalies:** each with its own look, sound and trap. Throw a bolt first.
- **A proper PDA:** map, tasks, statistics, relations, contacts, guide, radio and messages.
- **Emissions done right:** red sky, lightning, the wave, and your ears ringing after.
- **Cooking and a workbench** instead of furnaces and crafting tables.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.4 | 2026-11-02
- **Fixed:** item pictures were invisible in the inventory, loot screen, trader and quick slots.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.3 | 2026-11-02
Your own two hands: first person uses your skin's arms, blocky like the rest of the Zone.
- **Both hands are yours:** your skin and suit hold the gun, the detector and the PDA.
- **Fixed:** a third arm when aiming down the sights.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.2 | 2026-11-02
Into the Zone: first person, looks, mutants and sound the S.T.A.L.K.E.R. way.
- **Hands, not blocks:** gloved hands hold your guns, the knife, the PDA in both hands and a detector up in your left with a bolt in your right. Detectors show live readouts.
- **Factions look the part:** Loners, Bandits, Military, Duty, Freedom, Mercenaries, Monolith and Ecologists in their own suits, carrying real guns.
- **Mutants:** boars, mutant pigs, blind dog packs, an invisible hunter, gas-masked leapers, zombified stalkers, a psy master, a brute, a telekinetic and a two-headed cat.
- **The Zone's sound:** no music outdoors, only wind, crows, far gunfire and howls; sirens when an emission comes.
- **Darker and wetter:** shadows, fog, light shafts, near-black nights, rain puddles, and new ruined blocks and thin trees.
- **STALKER menus and a Misery loot screen,** all with full controller support.
## Exclusion 0.1.0 alpha.1 | 2026-11-02
First playable alpha of **Exclusion**, a survival shooter set in a ruined Exclusion Zone. Bring boots, bandages and a plan.
- **A huge Zone:** about 13 by 28 km of open land, from the south fence up to the plant, with villages, farms, rail yards, swamp, forest and the dead town beyond.
- **A-Life:** squads of stalkers, bandits, soldiers and mutants live in the Zone whether or not you are watching. They patrol, loot, fight each other and move on.
- **Guns with attachments you fit and strip:** every weapon takes optics, muzzles, grips and magazines, and comes apart on the workbench. Weapons and attachments come from Battle of Spades.
- **Misery-style weight and condition:** what you carry slows you down, rifles jam when they are dirty, armour and boots wear out, and wounds bleed until you bandage them.
- **Anomalies, artifacts and emissions:** throw a bolt before you step. Artifacts sit in the danger, and when the sky turns red you find cover or you do not wake up.
- **A bunker you dig out and furnish:** claim a ruined cellar, clear it, then make it yours with a stove, a bed, a workbench and a locked stash.
- **Split screen, LAN and online co-op:** two to four players on one screen, or a dedicated server from the launcher.
- **Full controller support** in every menu and in the field, with a rebindable layout.
- Removed Herobrine.
